# apps/web talks to the API through RELATIVE paths ('/api/...', '/socket.io'),
# proxied to the real API by Vite's dev server (see apps/web/vite.config.ts).
# There is therefore no VITE_API_URL / VITE_SOCKET_URL to set for the normal
# case — the browser only ever sees ONE origin, which is what lets the
# refresh-token cookie's SameSite=Strict actually work (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
# §7). Do not point this app at a different origin (an ngrok tunnel, a
# separate host/port with no reverse proxy) — that is cross-site, and the
# browser silently withholds the cookie, which looks exactly like "refresh
# doesn't work" with no error anywhere.
#
# If the API is not running on its default port (3000 — see the root .env),
# change vite.config.ts's API_TARGET, not a variable here.
